{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Rod</b> — a staff, and it is an allusion to the tongue, which is likened to a staff. That is, in the fool's mouth is a staff, namely the tongue, with which he strikes through words of pride." "<b>And the lips of the wise</b> — that they not speak with pride." "<b>Will guard them</b> — the lip will guard them, for it speaks concerning each one."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:38.112983532Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}